# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING IN data/ EVER GOES IN GIT.
#
# This used to read `data/*.db*`, which matches a file directly inside data/ and
# NOT one in a subdirectory. Since the move to one database per account the real
# records live in data/accounts/, so every patient database was about to be
# committed to a public repository. The whole directory is ignored now, because
# an allowlist of patterns is the wrong shape for this: a new subdirectory should
# be excluded by default, not included by default.
#
# ANCHORED, and that leading slash is load-bearing. Unanchored, `data/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed all of
# src/lib/data/ — the entire data-access layer, ten files the app cannot start
# without. Nothing failed locally, because the files were on disk; the repository
# simply did not contain them, so a fresh clone could not build. The anchored form
# still excludes every patient database, which is the whole point of the rule.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/

# Secrets. .env.example is the template and IS committed; it holds no values.
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
.env.production

# Local tooling and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.log

# Test and scratch output
coverage/
.fly/
